<title>AUSTRALIA: Australia govt to spend A$175 mln on rail upgrade.</title>
<headline>Australia govt to spend A$175 mln on rail upgrade.</headline>
<dateline>CANBERRA 1997-05-13</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Australian government said on Tuesday it would set aside A$175 million in the 1997/98 (July/June) fiscal year to upgrade mainline rail tracks.</p>
<p>It said the funds were part of plans to establish a national rail infrastructure network, which would be open to both government and private rail operators.</p>
<p>&quot;The A$175 million will contribute to investment in the interstate standard gauge track,&quot; Transport Minister John Sharp said in a statement. &quot;This will enable rail to compete more aggressively with road transport on the lucrative inter-capital freight journeys.&quot; -- Canberra Bureau 61-6 273-2730</p>
</text>
